recommend keep-going -- the honest next lap in this lane is the source's own port discovery, which my last lap named and this one did not touch: halving a shared resource is not removing it, so tools/fixtures/a/amphora_vessel_port_lock.sh still keeps two lawful runs from meeting. The ruling that stays Keaton's is unchanged from two laps back -- whether an OPEN row should carry a claim, a seat and a stamp at start, since a third pair of hands duplicated a peer's finding today.
